3.3.0 (not yet released)

#359: (blackbird) New code generation engine: per-bean codec classes, generated with
  the JDK ClassFile API, replace the LambdaMetafactory accessors. The codecs also
  cover records (through the canonical constructor) and builder-based beans.
  Blackbird needs Java 25 or later at run time: the generators use the ClassFile API
  (final in Java 24) and compile at release 25, the current LTS release. The jar is
  a multi-release jar whose base classes stay at Java 17: on Java 17-24, module
  discovery (`findAndAddModules()`) skips Blackbird with one logged warning, and an
  explicit `addModule(new BlackbirdModule())` throws `IllegalStateException`. The
  build needs JDK 25 for Blackbird, and a release build on an older JDK fails.
  Removed public types: `deser.CreatorOptimizer`, `deser.ObjBooleanConsumer`, the
  `ObjIntBiFunction`, `ObjLongBiFunction` and `ObjBooleanBiFunction` interfaces of
  `BBDeserializerModifier`, `ser.ToBooleanFunction`, and all of `util`
  (`CheckedFunction`, `CheckedSupplier`, `ReflectionHack`, `Sneaky`, `Unchecked`).
  `BBDeserializerModifier` and `BBSerializerModifier` take only the lookup function
  now. Blackbird no longer uses the lookup that `BlackbirdModule` constructors and
  `findLookup()` overrides supply. The OSGi bundle exports only
  `tools.jackson.module.blackbird`, as the JPMS module does.
 (contributed by @stevenschlansker)
#362: Bump `byte-buddy` dependency from 1.17.8 to 1.18.15

